# QM sim → user version (four layers, one sim per agent)

Full procedure, verify gates and output contract:
**`.cursor/commands/qm-sim-user-version.md`** — read it before editing. This
rule is the short form for when the command isn't invoked explicitly.

## What you are building

One sim → `Sims_user_versions/sim-use-builds/<same-basename>.html`, four layers
in order:

1. **Guided-inquiry flow** — authored from scratch (QM sims ship none):
   standalone `inqShow`/`setupChoiceCard`/`applyStepReveals`/`onStep`, the SME
   card grammar (FRAME + 3–5 questions, classical baseline first, resolving
   answers, neutral stems, zero choreography prose — canonical flows in
   `../Final_JEE_sims/Sim_use_version_skills/guided-inquiry/references/golden-flows.md`,
   which include three QM sims from this course).
2. **Controls tutorial** — purple callout walking every control/readout,
   hidden-until-its-turn, `__fullReset` wired additively to this sim's Reset id.
3. **Welcome overlay** — three glass mode cards over a per-sim hero canvas drawn
   from the sim's own equations, plus the read-aloud player. No auto-start speech.
4. **Voiceover + Auto** — Listen row, two-row guide nav, shared speech engine
   (`__makeCardVoice`); Auto narrates hands-free and never answers a prediction.

## Specification (single source of truth — copy blocks, don't re-derive)

- `../Final_JEE_sims/Sim_use_version_skills/guided-inquiry/` (SKILL + implementation)
- `../Final_JEE_sims/Sim_use_version_skills/controls-tutorial/` (§1–§4 base, §6 voice, §6.5 TTS pitfalls)
- `../Final_JEE_sims/Sim_use_version_skills/welcome-overlay/`

Validated exemplars: **QM pilot** → `Sims_user_versions/sim-use-builds/infinite-potential-well.html`
(primary template — copy its controller/bridge/pill-fix shape);
**JEE voice reference** → `../Final_JEE_sims/Module-01-Kinematics/C025-projectile-motion-ground-to-ground.html`;
**JEE full C-series build** → `../Final_JEE_sims/Module-13-Optics/C203-refraction-and-snells-law.html`.

## QM-specific (differs from the JEE fleet)

- **No `Shell`, no lecture mode, no existing cards** — don't hunt for them;
  the inquiry machinery is standalone and yours to insert.
- **Ids vary per sim** (reset/play/theme) — map them first, wire to what exists.
- **Feedback pill** (`#qfbPill`, z-index 99990) collides with the guide nav and
  the welcome overlay — apply the pilot's two-line CSS fix on the 6 sims that
  carry it.
- **FULL vs LIGHT** — no play control ⇒ welcome + controls + voice only; add an
  inquiry only if a genuine slider-prediction exists; never pad weak cards.
- **Three.js sims** — hoist wiring above `if(!window.THREE) return;` guards.

## Non-negotiable

- Never modify the original sim — `cp` first, edit only the copy. No git.
- Small targeted edits; never whole-file rewrites.
- Physics kernel byte-identical apart from the sanctioned deltas.
- Never reuse another sim's concept list, misconceptions, or card copy.

## Gates — all must pass before reporting

The three jsdom verifiers (guided-inquiry, controls-tutorial, welcome-overlay,
each with `--baseline`), `node --check` on every inline script, unique-id and
hook checks, and the **mandatory real-Chrome flow probe**
(`../Final_JEE_sims/tools/flow-probe.mjs`). Never ship with a lowered bar; if a
gate can't pass, stop and say why.
